cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Punjab Data Project: the imperial print register of British
  Punjab, 1910-1912
message: >-
  Citation is requested, not required. The data is released
  under CC0; please also cite the source record (see
  references, below).
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Thomas
    family-names: Graves
  - given-names: Emmett
    family-names: Davis
    name-suffix: Prof.
repository-code: 'https://github.com/tgraves719/Punjab-Data-Project'
url: 'https://tgraves719.github.io/Punjab-Data-Project/'
abstract: >-
  A machine-readable dataset derived from the quarterly
  Catalogue of Books registered in the Punjab, compiled under
  Act XXV of 1867 and Act X of 1890. Covers twelve consecutive
  quarters, 1910-1912: 4,502 structured bibliographic entries
  recording 6,944,051 registered copies, across 350 printers,
  1,726 publishers and 59 printing cities, in Urdu, Punjabi,
  Hindi, English, Sindhi, Arabic, Persian and thirty further
  languages and script combinations. Every record retains the
  catalogue's own wording verbatim beside a normalised analytic
  layer, and links to the scanned page it came from. Built
  from India Office Records SV 412/44, Punjab, Vol 13.
keywords:
  - book history
  - South Asia
  - Punjab
  - colonial India
  - print culture
  - Urdu
  - digital humanities
  - historical bibliography
  - computational social science
license:
  - CC0-1.0
  - GPL-3.0-or-later
  - CC-BY-4.0
references:
  - type: report
    title: >-
      Catalogue of Books registered in the Punjab under Act XXV
      of 1867 and Act X of 1890
    authors:
      - name: Government of the Punjab, Education Department
    institution:
      name: British Library, India Office Records
    collection-title: 'India Office Records SV 412/44, Punjab, Vol 13'
    year: 1912
    notes: >-
      Quarterly. The full Punjab run is 26 bound volumes,
      1867-1942.
